  "question": {
    "text": "A certain charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is divided into two parts <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math> How should the charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> be divided so that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></math> placed at a certain distance apart experience maximum electrostatic repulsion?"
  },
